Q: Codeigniter SUM and LEFT JOIN while removing duplicates A: <pre><code>$this-&gt;db-&gt;select('COALESCE(SUM(cust_ reservation_request.dollar_amount), &quot;0&quot;) as total');
    $this-&gt;db-&gt;where exists (select 1 from cust_reservations where  cust_reservations.rid = cust_ reservation_request.id);
    $this-&gt;db-&gt;and exists (select 1 from attendees where cust.rid = cust_reservation_request.id); 
    $this-&gt;db-&gt;and exists (select 1 from cust_ reservation_cancelled where cust_reservation_cancelled.rid = cust_reservation_request.id);
    $this-&gt;db-&gt;and ('cust_ reservation_request.tid IN (5, 6, 7, 8)-&gt;where('attendees.status', 1)-&gt;where('cust_reservation_cancelled.rid IS NULL');
    $this-&gt;db-&gt;group_by('cust_reservation_request.id');
    $total = $this-&gt;db-&gt;get('cust_reservations')-&gt;row()-&gt;total;
</code></pre>
<p>Check the syntax and all the <code>()</code> and <code>'</code> as I only know plain SQL. You might have to change <code>and exists</code> in <code>where exists</code> and/or change a <code>where</code> later into an <code>and</code>.</p>
<p>This sums the dollar_amount from one table only (cust_ reservation_request) where you are sure that there also exists a row in the other tables with the same row_id.</p>
